---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';

/**
 * Category-level list referenced by /dpa §6.
 *
 * The messaging provider is a CATEGORY here — "messaging infrastructure
 * providers (EU-hosted)" — never a vendor name. That is defensible under
 * Art 13(1)(e) ("categories of recipients") and it is honest: it says the data
 * goes somewhere beyond the messaging platform, which is the fact that matters.
 * What is NOT permitted is implying it goes only to Meta.
 */
---

<Legal
  title="Sub-processors"
  description="The categories of service provider iGrowFast uses to process personal data on behalf of its customers, with regions and data types."
  path="/sub-processors"
  updated="16 July 2026"
  summary="Who else touches the data we process for you, what they handle, and where they are."
>
  <h2 id="about">About this list</h2>
  <p>
    This supports section 6 of our <a href="/dpa">Data Processing Addendum</a>.
    It lists sub-processors <strong>by category</strong>, with the region and the
    data each handles.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Why categories.</strong> Specific vendors within a category change,
    and a published list of brand names is out of date the week after it ships.
    What matters for your assessment is what leaves your control, where it goes,
    and under what terms — that is what this table tells you. If you are a
    customer and need the current named list for your own records or for your own
    customers' notices, ask us and we will provide it under the DPA. We answer
    that question; we just don't publish it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="list">Current sub-processors</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Category</th><th>What it handles</th><th>Data</th><th>Region</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Hosting and compute</strong></td>
          <td>Runs the application and the database — everything in the product passes through here</td>
          <td>All personal data in the product</td>
          <td>Germany</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Object storage and backups</strong></td>
          <td>Uploaded files, message media, encrypted database backups</td>
          <td>Media, attachments, full backups</td>
          <td>European Union</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Messaging infrastructure providers</strong></td>
          <td>Sending and receiving messages on your business's numbers</td>
          <td>Message content and metadata; phone numbers; contact names; media</td>
          <td>European Union</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Network, CDN and abuse protection</strong></td>
          <td>Routing, TLS termination, bot challenges on sign-in</td>
          <td>IP address, request metadata</td>
          <td>Global edge network</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Transactional email delivery</strong></td>
          <td>Account emails, invitations, statements, alerts</td>
          <td>Email address, name, message content</td>
          <td>European Union</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Email verification</strong></td>
          <td>Checking an address is deliverable at signup</td>
          <td>Email address only</td>
          <td>European Union / United States</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="not-yet">Configured but not active</h2>
  <p>
    These are described so this page is accurate the day they are enabled — and
    so you are not surprised. None currently receives any data.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Status</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Analytics and advertising</strong></td>
          <td><span class="wip">Not yet active</span></td>
          <td>Website measurement only, on <a href="/cookies">consent</a>. Does not touch product data or your customers' data.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>AI providers</strong></td>
          <td><span class="wip">Not yet in production</span></td>
          <td>Not currently used. If introduced, this list is updated and you are notified in advance under DPA §6 before any data reaches them.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="carriers">Carriers and platforms you connect yourself</h2>
  <p>
    When you connect a courier, a messaging platform, an advertising account or a
    spreadsheet, data flows to a provider <strong>you</strong> have a
    relationship with, on your instruction. Those are not our sub-processors —
    they are your own processors, and their terms are between you and them. We
    pass data to them because you told us to.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We give reasonable advance notice before adding or replacing a sub-processor.
    You may object on reasonable data protection grounds; if we can't resolve it,
    you may terminate the affected part of the service without penalty. See
    <a href="/dpa#subprocessors">DPA §6</a>.
  </p>
  <p>To be notified of changes, or to request the named list: <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.</p>
</Legal>
